I started playing hack on sunos back in 1990, of course it was
ASCII.  Along the way I discovered the nh10 font for the X11
interface and liked it a lot.  My reason for liking it is the little
glyphs are more descriptive... you can easily tell a bag from a box,
they aren't both just '('s.  So I liked the additional information
I was getting wihtout having to waste keystrokes id'ing an object
in the map.

I tried with 32x32 tiles sometime back and disliked them because they were
too big... you couldn't see the entire map on the screen at the same
time and that really bugged me.  As well, tiles for character status seems
a waste of screen space.

However, I wouldn't trade nh10 font for ascii... I'd probably quit
playing instead.

Of course, the beauty of it is that its up to the user - its
personal preference and the game supports a lot of different
modes.

But I'd be interested to hear rather than _if_ people prefer X over Y,
_why_ they prefer X over Y.  I've told mine - tiles are too big that
you can't see enough, ascii doesn't deliver enough information.

Anyone else?  (BTW, is nh10 font a "tile" or not?  Am I playing
ASCII or Tile? :) )

